1
00:00:03,461 --> 00:00:06,255
Hello, I'm Dr. Sheldon Cooper.

2
00:00:06,422 --> 00:00:10,259
Welcome to
Sheldon Cooper Presents Fun With Flags.

3
00:00:11,844 --> 00:00:12,928
Before we get started...

4
00:00:13,095 --> 00:00:16,765
...I'd like to announce the winner of our
"design your own flag" competition...

5
00:00:16,933 --> 00:00:18,601
_but |I can't.

6
00:00:18,768 --> 00:00:23,268
The only entry was from GameyGamer75,
I know that was a JPEG of your buttocks.

7
00:00:25,483 --> 00:00:28,277
Now, this week,
we have a very special episode...

8
00:00:28,444 --> 00:00:32,944
...where we explore the flags of the popular
entertainment franchise Star Trek.

9
00:00:33,115 --> 00:00:37,077
And to help me, I'm pleased to introduce
Internet personality...

10
00:00:37,245 --> 00:00:39,997
...former star of
Star Trek: The Next Generation. ..

11
00:00:40,164 --> 00:00:44,664
...and the only guy I know lucky enough
to be immortalized in one-sixteenth scale.

12
00:00:45,670 --> 00:00:48,005
Set phasers to "fun”...

13
00:00:50,758 --> 00:00:53,135
...for my friend Wil Wheaton.

14
00:00:55,179 --> 00:00:57,723
-Hi, thanks for having me. Happy to be here.
AMY: Cut.

15
00:00:59,517 --> 00:01:02,978
-What's wrong?
-Sorry, you were brilliant as always.

16
00:01:03,145 --> 00:01:05,397
Wil, that was a little wooden.

17
00:01:06,983 --> 00:01:09,151
-Wooden?
-Don't worry, it wasn't terrible.

18
00:01:09,318 --> 00:01:13,030
Just this time,
try to say it the way people sound.

19
00:01:14,907 --> 00:01:16,533
And action.

20
00:01:17,326 --> 00:01:18,994
My friend Wil Wheaton.

21
00:01:19,161 --> 00:01:21,496
Hi, thanks for having me.
I'm excited to be here.

22
00:01:21,664 --> 00:01:26,043
-So, Wil, what do you have for us first?
-Well, this is an exciting one.

23
00:01:26,210 --> 00:01:28,670
This is the flag
of the United Federation of Planets.

24
00:01:28,838 --> 00:01:31,632
-Now, what's interesting about this flag--
AMY: Cut.

25
00:01:32,633 --> 00:01:36,553
-What was wrong with that?
-It's called Fun With Flags.

26
00:01:36,721 --> 00:01:40,433
They're not at half-mast. Nobody died.
Let's try and keep it upbeat.

27
00:01:41,601 --> 00:01:44,979
Um, no offense,
but I've been acting since I was a kid.

28
00:01:45,146 --> 00:01:47,565
I can handle a web show
without a lot of direction.

29
00:01:47,732 --> 00:01:48,774
SHELDON:
It's true.

30
00:01:49,025 --> 00:01:53,029
In 1982 Wil played the voice
of Martin the mouse in The Secret of NIMH.

31
00:01:53,571 --> 00:01:54,947
You moved me.

32
00:01:56,032 --> 00:01:57,408
You'll have to forgive me.

33
00:01:57,575 --> 00:02:00,744
This is my first time directing.
I just want it to be good.

34
00:02:00,953 --> 00:02:02,204
-So do I.
AMY: Great.

35
00:02:02,371 --> 00:02:05,749
So this time, let's try more real boy,
less Pinocchio.

36
00:02:07,752 --> 00:02:09,879
-And action.
-And cut.

37
00:02:11,088 --> 00:02:13,256
You realize I'm doing this for free, right?

38
00:02:13,466 --> 00:02:17,094
Yes, and so far,
we're still not getting our money's worth.

39
00:02:19,764 --> 00:02:21,599
Let's try it again.

40
00:02:21,766 --> 00:02:23,893
Everybody's having fun.

41
00:02:24,393 --> 00:02:26,061
And action.

42
00:02:26,228 --> 00:02:27,896
So, WII...

43
00:02:35,780 --> 00:02:38,365
...what do you have for us first?

44
00:02:38,532 --> 00:02:41,785
Well, this is an exciting one.

45
00:02:41,994 --> 00:02:45,622
This is the flag
of the United Federation of Planets.

46
00:02:45,790 --> 00:02:46,916
Cut.

47
00:02:47,583 --> 00:02:49,668
Problem, first-time director?

48
00:02:50,544 --> 00:02:51,711
None that I could see.

49
00:02:51,879 --> 00:02:54,423
I saw a man who loved flags
almost as much as I do.

50
00:02:54,590 --> 00:02:56,925
I got goose bumps.

51
00:02:57,093 --> 00:03:00,262
-He was overacting on purpose.
-Really?

52
00:03:00,429 --> 00:03:03,223
Oh, he reminded me
of a young William Shatner.

53
00:03:04,392 --> 00:03:06,143
I'm really happy to do this for you...

54
00:03:06,310 --> 00:03:09,771
...but not if she's gonna be a huge
pain in the ass the whole time.

55
00:03:10,314 --> 00:03:12,899
Are you gonna let him speak to me
like that?

56
00:03:13,067 --> 00:03:14,735
Well. ..

57
00:03:16,362 --> 00:03:19,365
...you're my girlfriend,
and I don't want you to be upset.

58
00:03:20,032 --> 00:03:23,452
Then again, Wil Wheaton's my friend,
and I don't want him to be upset.

59
00:03:23,619 --> 00:03:25,412
Hmm. ...

60
00:03:25,579 --> 00:03:26,955
This is a sticky wicket.

61
00:03:28,708 --> 00:03:30,042
What do you think?

62
00:03:31,043 --> 00:03:33,003
Can I speak to you for a second?

63
00:03:33,170 --> 00:03:34,921
I'll be right back.

64
00:03:35,089 --> 00:03:36,965
Feel free to play with yourself.

65
00:03:43,973 --> 00:03:46,934
I don't care for your friend,
and he's being rude to me.

66
00:03:47,101 --> 00:03:48,435
You need to ask him to leave.

67
00:03:48,602 --> 00:03:51,396
Amy, I can't just ask Wil Wheaton to leave.

68
00:03:51,564 --> 00:03:53,232
He's a minor celebrity.

69
00:03:54,483 --> 00:03:57,611
Once you explain who he is,
many people recognize him.

70
00:03:58,696 --> 00:04:00,072
Fine, then maybe I should go.

71
00:04:00,573 --> 00:04:02,408
Could you? That would solve everything.

72
00:04:04,702 --> 00:04:08,122
You are the best.
I'll see you at dinner tonight?

73
00:04:08,289 --> 00:04:11,375
Sure you wouldn't rather have dinner
with your friend Wil Wheaton?

74
00:04:11,542 --> 00:04:13,627
Come to think of it, I would.

75
00:04:14,545 --> 00:04:17,005
You, little lady, are on fire.

76
00:04:44,784 --> 00:04:48,120
Every time we eat here, your mom refuses
to let me help with the dishes.

77
00:04:48,287 --> 00:04:49,496
Don't take it personally.

78
00:04:49,663 --> 00:04:53,667
She likes doing them by herself so she can
lick the plates with no one looking.

79
00:04:54,418 --> 00:04:55,585
You ready to go?

80
00:04:55,753 --> 00:05:00,007
Yeah, let me just grab a couple
of fresh turtlenecks.

81
00:05:00,174 --> 00:05:03,760
I don't understand why you keep your stuff
here when there's room at home.

82
00:05:03,928 --> 00:05:05,179
What are you talking about?

83
00:05:05,429 --> 00:05:09,558
All I have here is a few sweaters,
books, bank stuff...

84
00:05:09,725 --> 00:05:13,103
...computers, mail, collectibles, medicine
and my electric body groomer.

85
00:05:14,897 --> 00:05:17,649
Ooh! There's my plaid dickey.

86
00:05:17,817 --> 00:05:22,317
Oh. Got this at the Goodwill store for 50 cents.
Can you believe it? Heh.

87
00:05:24,490 --> 00:05:26,700
Fifty cents sounds right.

88
00:05:28,536 --> 00:05:30,788
-Let's go.
-You know, it's kind of late.

89
00:05:30,955 --> 00:05:33,958
-Why don't we spend the night here?
-Because we don't live here.

90
00:05:34,124 --> 00:05:35,667
- I know.
-Do you?

91
00:05:35,835 --> 00:05:37,711
You said when you got back from space...

92
00:05:37,878 --> 00:05:41,256
...you were gonna move into my apartment,
but half the time we stay here.

93
00:05:41,423 --> 00:05:42,882
That's not true.

94
00:05:43,133 --> 00:05:47,387
MRS. WOLOWITZ: Howard, I'm doing laundry!
You want me to put anything in for you?!

95
00:05:47,555 --> 00:05:50,641
There's some underwear in the hamper!

96
00:05:51,100 --> 00:05:53,894
MRS. WOLOWITZ:
Oh, good, I got that new stain stick to try out!

97
00:05:56,689 --> 00:06:00,275
Thank you.
I only put it on the list two weeks ago!

98
00:06:01,735 --> 00:06:03,528
Okay, I see what you're getting at.

99
00:06:04,822 --> 00:06:09,076
How about this weekend,
I'll box up all my things...

100
00:06:09,243 --> 00:06:11,662
...and move them to our place?

101
00:06:11,829 --> 00:06:13,163
Thank you.

102
00:06:13,330 --> 00:06:15,832
The lightsabers will look great
in the living room.

103
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:18,877
Or in the closet. We can decide later.

104
00:06:20,004 --> 00:06:23,924
MRS. WOLOWITZ: Howard, help!
My hand's stuck in the garbage disposal!

105
00:06:24,174 --> 00:06:28,094
Just let go of whatever piece of food
you're holding!

106
00:06:28,762 --> 00:06:33,057
MRS. WOLOWITZ: Are you kidding?!
It's a perfectly good chicken leg!

107
00:06:35,519 --> 00:06:38,438
Hey, look who's out after dark
like a big boy.

108
00:06:39,565 --> 00:06:42,317
I was out raising heck
with Mr. Wil Wheaton.

109
00:06:42,484 --> 00:06:46,321
Four hours more and we would have
closed down the HomeTown Buffet.

110
00:06:47,072 --> 00:06:49,282
-I thought you had plans with Amy.
-Yeah, I did.

111
00:06:49,450 --> 00:06:52,786
But then Wil called Amy a pain in the A-S-S.

112
00:06:53,787 --> 00:06:56,998
She got huffy and left,
and then Wil and I headed out to dinner.

113
00:06:57,166 --> 00:07:01,044
That place really did remind me
of my hometown.

114
00:07:01,211 --> 00:07:03,713
Because there we also have
a HomeTown Buffet.

115
00:07:06,133 --> 00:07:10,303
-Hold on. Wil and Amy had an argument?
-Yes, quite the kerfuffle.

116
00:07:10,471 --> 00:07:14,266
-Then Amy got mad and left?
-Walked right out the door.

117
00:07:14,433 --> 00:07:15,976
And you...?

118
00:07:16,143 --> 00:07:18,812
Enjoyed a delightful dinner
at a reasonable price.

119
00:07:20,064 --> 00:07:24,564
The manager recognized Wil and let us sit
right next to the frozen-yogurt machine.

120
00:07:24,818 --> 00:07:26,110
Right next to it.

121
00:07:26,612 --> 00:07:29,656
I was closer to it than I am to you right now.

122
00:07:31,992 --> 00:07:35,620
-Buddy, I think Amy might be upset.
-Why's that?

123
00:07:35,788 --> 00:07:39,333
Because your friend was rude to her
and then you went to dinner with him.

124
00:07:39,875 --> 00:07:42,502
You're just repeating what I said.

125
00:07:42,670 --> 00:07:45,547
It's like living
with a lactose-intolerant parrot.

126
00:07:47,841 --> 00:07:49,634
Trust me. Call her.

127
00:07:50,094 --> 00:07:51,428
Fine.

128
00:07:51,595 --> 00:07:53,805
It's a shame you didn't go
to dinner with us. ..

129
00:07:53,973 --> 00:07:57,142
...because the buffet you're about to enjoy
only serves humble pie...

130
00:07:57,309 --> 00:07:59,936
...a dessert much less tasty
than frozen yogurt.

131
00:08:00,104 --> 00:08:01,355
I was this close.

132
00:08:04,942 --> 00:08:06,693
What?

133
00:08:07,611 --> 00:08:08,695
You'll appreciate this.

134
00:08:08,862 --> 00:08:11,531
Leonard has some ridiculous notion
that you're mad at me.

135
00:08:11,699 --> 00:08:14,702
Tell him you're not mad at me.
Go ahead, set him straight.

136
00:08:14,868 --> 00:08:16,369
I'm mad at you, Sheldon.

137
00:08:17,329 --> 00:08:18,788
Hmm. ...

138
00:08:18,956 --> 00:08:20,624
Eat one of your Luna Bars.

139
00:08:22,459 --> 00:08:25,962
Very often, when women think
they're angry, they're really just hungry.

140
00:08:27,548 --> 00:08:29,007
I'm not hungry.

141
00:08:29,883 --> 00:08:32,218
Your friend insulted me
and you didn't do anything.

142
00:08:32,386 --> 00:08:36,056
Precisely. I didn't do anything.

143
00:08:37,141 --> 00:08:40,018
Now, does someone feel like checking
her emotional math?

144
00:08:40,728 --> 00:08:43,230
Keep going, buddy. You're doing great.

145
00:08:43,939 --> 00:08:47,067
Sheldon, I'm your girlfriend
and you should have taken my side.

146
00:08:47,234 --> 00:08:50,695
That's it. End of story. Good night.

147
00:08:51,947 --> 00:08:56,447
Wow, Amy's mad and Leonard was right.

148
00:08:57,077 --> 00:08:59,079
What a weird day.

149
00:09:01,540 --> 00:09:04,084
Hey, sorry this took so long.
But you used to work here.

150
00:09:04,251 --> 00:09:06,920
-You know how it is.
-Kitchen slammed again?

151
00:09:07,087 --> 00:09:09,255
No, I'm a terrible waitress, remember?

152
00:09:11,091 --> 00:09:13,343
So anything I can do
to help you move tomorrow?

153
00:09:13,510 --> 00:09:17,764
Now that you mention it,
I was thinking tomorrow might not be great.

154
00:09:18,307 --> 00:09:20,934
-What's your excuse this time?
-No excuse.

155
00:09:21,101 --> 00:09:22,727
It's just, you know, I'm Jewish...

156
00:09:22,895 --> 00:09:26,773
...and technically, we're not supposed
to drive or carry anything on the Sabbath...

157
00:09:26,940 --> 00:09:28,775
50 this one's on God.

158
00:09:29,860 --> 00:09:34,114
That might be more convincing if you didn't
have a mouthful of bacon cheeseburger.

159
00:09:34,948 --> 00:09:37,575
My religion's kind of loosey-goosey,
you know.

160
00:09:37,743 --> 00:09:41,997
As long as you got your schmeckel
clipped and don't wear a cross, you're good.

161
00:09:43,791 --> 00:09:45,375
Howie, you promised you'd move.

162
00:09:45,542 --> 00:09:47,919
-And I will.
-Yeah, right.

163
00:09:48,087 --> 00:09:52,587
I'm not going to live in my mother's house
for the rest of my life. I'm not a child.

164
00:09:53,509 --> 00:09:55,802
I've seen her burp you.

165
00:09:58,806 --> 00:09:59,890
She did not burp me.

166
00:10:00,057 --> 00:10:03,268
She was patting me on the back
and I happened to burp.

167
00:10:05,729 --> 00:10:08,148
Don't you have other tables
you should be waiting on?

168
00:10:08,315 --> 00:10:10,734
Yeah, but I told you, I'm not good at my job.

169
00:10:11,443 --> 00:10:15,447
-Listen to me. He is never gonna leave.
-I'm starting to think you're right.

170
00:10:15,614 --> 00:10:19,659
All right, I've had enough of this.
I'm a grown man. I have a successful career.

171
00:10:19,910 --> 00:10:22,162
I mean, for the love of God,
I've been to space.

172
00:10:22,412 --> 00:10:26,165
I will move out when I'm ready, and I don't
need anyone badgering me into it.

173
00:10:26,875 --> 00:10:29,335
Wow. Excuse me.

174
00:10:30,796 --> 00:10:34,674
That was just for her benefit. I'll move
tomorrow. I love you. Don't leave me.

175
00:10:39,221 --> 00:10:40,680
Amy?

176
00:10:40,848 --> 00:10:42,266
Amy.

177
00:10:42,850 --> 00:10:44,560
Angry Amy?

178
00:10:46,520 --> 00:10:47,604
What?

179
00:10:48,105 --> 00:10:52,605
I've been thinking about what happened,
and I hope this gift will make things better.

180
00:10:56,697 --> 00:10:59,199
Star Trek DVDs?

181
00:10:59,366 --> 00:11:00,700
Why would I want this?

182
00:11:01,368 --> 00:11:02,702
First of all, you're welcome.

183
00:11:04,037 --> 00:11:07,290
Furthermore, not being familiar
with Wil Wheaton's body of work...

184
00:11:07,457 --> 00:11:11,502
...there was no way for you to know
you were being rude to a national treasure.

185
00:11:12,337 --> 00:11:15,340
Get ready for 130 hours of "I told you so."

186
00:11:20,387 --> 00:11:22,764
Fine, I'll just tell you what happens.

187
00:11:23,473 --> 00:11:26,601
Episode one, "Encounter at Farpoint.”

188
00:11:26,768 --> 00:11:27,852
Fade in.

189
00:11:28,020 --> 00:11:30,480
The new Enterprise heads out
on its maiden voyage...

190
00:11:30,647 --> 00:11:33,107
...to contact the Bandi people of Deneb IV.

191
00:11:33,275 --> 00:11:36,736
Enter Wesley Crusher,
played by my buddy--

192
00:11:40,991 --> 00:11:42,742
She's hooked.

193
00:11:52,377 --> 00:11:54,879
Wow, an end of an era.

194
00:11:55,547 --> 00:11:59,092
Boy, if these walls could talk.

195
00:12:00,177 --> 00:12:03,305
They'd say,
"Why does he touch himself so much?"

196
00:12:08,602 --> 00:12:09,686
Yeah.

197
00:12:12,105 --> 00:12:15,399
I can't believe
I'm not gonna live here anymore.

198
00:12:15,651 --> 00:12:18,904
This has always been my bedroom.

199
00:12:19,071 --> 00:12:22,657
Right here is where my mom
used to mark my height.

200
00:12:22,824 --> 00:12:24,408
Oh, yeah.

201
00:12:24,576 --> 00:12:29,076
"Fifth grade, sixth grade,
seventh grade, eighth grade, ninth grade.”

202
00:12:32,084 --> 00:12:35,253
Yeah, I remember when I was 5...

203
00:12:35,420 --> 00:12:38,756
...hiding under this desk
with all my Halloween candy.

204
00:12:39,341 --> 00:12:41,551
Had some Peanut M&M's...

205
00:12:41,718 --> 00:12:46,218
...went into my first anaphylactic shock,
had to be rushed to the hospital...

206
00:12:47,015 --> 00:12:50,768
...came home, celebrated with a Snickers,
went into my second anaphylactic shock.

207
00:12:52,980 --> 00:12:55,190
When did you figure out
you're allergic to nuts?

208
00:12:55,357 --> 00:12:57,192
Sometime around the third Almond Joy.

209
00:12:59,278 --> 00:13:01,863
Okay, wanna start loading this stuff
into the truck?

210
00:13:02,030 --> 00:13:03,906
Yeah, I guess.

211
00:13:04,074 --> 00:13:06,576
Hey, would you do me a favor?
Go on ahead.

212
00:13:06,743 --> 00:13:11,243
I just want one last moment alone
in my old room.

213
00:13:11,790 --> 00:13:15,710
We're not standing outside by the U-Haul
while you fondle yourself.

214
00:13:15,919 --> 00:13:17,253
[SCOFFS]

215
00:13:18,588 --> 00:13:19,672
Fine, let's go.

216
00:13:26,471 --> 00:13:29,223
Hey, what brings you in?

217
00:13:29,391 --> 00:13:33,891
Penny, if you wouldn't mind,
I'd like to have a conversation about girls.

218
00:13:36,064 --> 00:13:39,650
Had a feeling we'd have a talk like this
sooner or later.

219
00:13:39,818 --> 00:13:43,571
Are you finally getting fuzz in weird places?

220
00:13:43,739 --> 00:13:47,701
Penny, please, I'm on the horns
of a relationship dilemma.

221
00:13:47,868 --> 00:13:51,705
And for the record, I had a full pubis of hair
by the time I was 19.

222
00:13:53,832 --> 00:13:54,874
And for the record:

223
00:13:55,042 --> 00:13:56,501
[I MIMICS VOMITING]

224
00:13:57,878 --> 00:14:00,797
-So, what are you drinking?
-Well, it's been a rough day.

225
00:14:00,964 --> 00:14:04,175
I usually go chamomile tea,
but I don't think that's gonna cut it.

226
00:14:04,760 --> 00:14:07,596
You could have a Long Island iced tea.

227
00:14:10,807 --> 00:14:13,142
Will that calm my nerves?

228
00:14:13,852 --> 00:14:17,230
It's calmed the pants off me a couple times.

229
00:14:18,231 --> 00:14:20,775
-Sold.
-Oh.

230
00:14:21,234 --> 00:14:25,196
So the heart you got from the wizard
giving you trouble?

231
00:14:25,364 --> 00:14:28,492
The trouble isn't with me, Penny,
it's with your gender.

232
00:14:28,658 --> 00:14:30,326
Someday scientists will discover...

233
00:14:30,494 --> 00:14:34,748
...that second X chromosome contains
nothing but nonsense and twaddle.

234
00:14:35,207 --> 00:14:37,042
Yeah, Amy told me what happened.

235
00:14:37,209 --> 00:14:40,754
Look, just apologize. It'll warm her twaddle.

236
00:14:41,505 --> 00:14:43,173
That's a Band-Aid at best.

237
00:14:43,340 --> 00:14:46,801
The core problem is that Amy and Wil
do not like each other. ..

238
00:14:46,968 --> 00:14:50,388
...which is baffling
because they're both crazy about me.

239
00:14:51,848 --> 00:14:55,184
And I like them, which indicates
they're bright and interesting...

240
00:14:55,352 --> 00:14:57,729
_and/or were on Star Trek.

241
00:14:58,647 --> 00:15:00,774
Honey, you can't make people
like each other.

242
00:15:01,233 --> 00:15:04,319
Not true. Leonard made me like you.

243
00:15:04,486 --> 00:15:06,654
Let me tell you, that was a hard row to hoe.

244
00:15:08,198 --> 00:15:10,116
Cheers, pal.

245
00:15:11,910 --> 00:15:13,745
Ooh!

246
00:15:14,162 --> 00:15:17,165
Boy, that is a treat that's hard to beat.

247
00:15:18,750 --> 00:15:21,836
Get the Mad Hatter on the horn.
I'm having a tea party.

248
00:15:27,467 --> 00:15:29,051
You might wanna pace yourself.

249
00:15:30,011 --> 00:15:33,222
I drink tea all the time.
I think I know what I'm doing.

250
00:15:34,307 --> 00:15:37,435
Far be it for me
to criticize a man with a full pubis.

251
00:15:40,147 --> 00:15:44,526
Look, your problem is not Wil Wheaton.
Your problem is the way you treated Amy.

252
00:15:44,693 --> 00:15:47,112
Problem is I'm out of tea.

253
00:15:48,488 --> 00:15:51,699
Come on, someone insulted your girlfriend,
you just let him do it?

254
00:15:51,867 --> 00:15:54,536
Thought you Texas guys stood up
for your womenfolk.

255
00:15:54,703 --> 00:15:56,371
Oh, Penny, please.

256
00:15:56,538 --> 00:15:59,624
Think I've evolved
beyond my simple rustic upbringing.

257
00:15:59,791 --> 00:16:00,875
Sorry.

258
00:16:01,042 --> 00:16:05,004
On the other hand, that low-down polecat
done wronged my woman.

259
00:16:08,133 --> 00:16:10,885
Welcome to Long Island, Tex.

260
00:16:12,262 --> 00:16:13,930
Amy deserves better.

261
00:16:14,097 --> 00:16:16,474
You know,
when we buy the Planters Deluxe Mix...

262
00:16:16,641 --> 00:16:19,935
...she eats all the Brazil nuts
so I don't have to look at them.

263
00:16:21,563 --> 00:16:24,440
She's a unique blend of saint and squirrel.

264
00:16:25,233 --> 00:16:27,818
Yup, that she is. Here you go.

265
00:16:27,986 --> 00:16:31,531
I'm a callous egomaniac.
She's gonna leave me.

266
00:16:31,698 --> 00:16:34,742
-No, she won't.
-No, she won't. I'm great.

267
00:16:43,168 --> 00:16:44,627
Ah!

268
00:16:46,087 --> 00:16:50,587
Okay, I have now officially moved out
of my mother's house.

269
00:16:51,426 --> 00:16:55,012
You are now the only woman in my life
who I'll see naked in the bathroom.

270
00:16:56,097 --> 00:16:58,641
I know this wasn't easy. You doing okay?

271
00:16:58,808 --> 00:17:02,102
Well, I'm fine. It's just her I'm worried about.

272
00:17:02,646 --> 00:17:05,815
-She'll be okay. She's a grown woman.
- I know.

273
00:17:05,982 --> 00:17:10,482
It's just ever since my dad left,
I've felt responsible for her.

274
00:17:11,238 --> 00:17:13,198
That's a lot for a kid to deal with.

275
00:17:13,365 --> 00:17:16,117
She was just so sad all the time.

276
00:17:16,284 --> 00:17:19,287
I was the only person
who could cheer her up.

277
00:17:19,454 --> 00:17:21,706
Well, me and Ben and Jerry.

278
00:17:23,124 --> 00:17:25,167
She's lucky you were there.

279
00:17:27,087 --> 00:17:30,298
You know, she's why I first got into magic.

280
00:17:30,465 --> 00:17:32,133
I would do little shows for her.

281
00:17:32,300 --> 00:17:36,800
Hang up a bed sheet like it was a curtain,
put on a top hat and cape.

282
00:17:37,639 --> 00:17:42,139
And partway through the act, I would say
I needed a volunteer from the audience. ..

283
00:17:43,311 --> 00:17:47,811
...to be my beautiful assistant
and invite her up on-stage.

284
00:17:49,484 --> 00:17:52,987
I can still remember the way she'd smile.

285
00:17:53,572 --> 00:17:58,072
For a few minutes,
she'd forget how lonely she was.

286
00:18:00,579 --> 00:18:03,373
Aw, crap. Let's go.

287
00:18:04,541 --> 00:18:05,833
Where are we going?

288
00:18:06,001 --> 00:18:08,545
Grab a box.
We'll sleep at your mother's place tonight.

289
00:18:08,712 --> 00:18:10,422
No, but I want to live here.

290
00:18:10,589 --> 00:18:14,676
Well, you should've thought of that before
you told me the stupid magic-trick story.

291
00:18:15,552 --> 00:18:17,220
Can't we talk about this?

292
00:18:17,387 --> 00:18:21,474
No husband of mine
IS gonna break his mother's heart.

293
00:18:28,398 --> 00:18:30,108
Wil Wheaton.

294
00:18:30,275 --> 00:18:32,110
Wil Wheaton.

295
00:18:33,028 --> 00:18:35,030
Wait, how many was that?

296
00:18:37,824 --> 00:18:42,078
-Hey, Sheldon, what's up?
-Wouldn't you like to know.

297
00:18:43,371 --> 00:18:46,582
-Have you been drinking?
-Just tea.

298
00:18:47,500 --> 00:18:50,294
It was the best tea |I've ever had.

299
00:18:51,713 --> 00:18:53,047
Why are you here?

300
00:18:53,715 --> 00:18:55,174
I'll tell you.

301
00:18:55,342 --> 00:18:57,552
I'm from Texas.

302
00:18:58,053 --> 00:19:00,513
Need I say more?

303
00:19:01,640 --> 00:19:04,309
Yeah, actually,
a little more would be helpful.

304
00:19:04,476 --> 00:19:08,976
You insulted my woman.
I'm here to defend her honor.

305
00:19:09,230 --> 00:19:10,648
Two. It was two.

306
00:19:11,316 --> 00:19:13,401
Wil Wheaton.

307
00:19:15,904 --> 00:19:19,657
Now prepare yourself for what may come.

308
00:19:22,243 --> 00:19:24,954
Oh, Sheldon,
do you really think we're gonna fight?

309
00:19:25,121 --> 00:19:29,291
My fists are not up here
because I'm milking a giant invisible cow.

310
00:19:31,211 --> 00:19:34,255
They're up to beat an apology out of you.

311
00:19:35,090 --> 00:19:36,466
Okay, I'm sorry.

312
00:19:37,592 --> 00:19:40,136
Well, that was a long bus ride
for not very much.

313
00:19:41,638 --> 00:19:42,722
Are you okay?

314
00:19:42,889 --> 00:19:45,516
You're asking a lot of questions,
Wil Wheaton.

315
00:19:45,684 --> 00:19:47,394
As a matter of idle curiosity...

316
00:19:47,560 --> 00:19:52,060
...which of your shrubberies do you feel
would benefit from a thorough vomiting?

317
00:19:52,774 --> 00:19:54,776
Never mind, I'll choose.

318
00:19:56,569 --> 00:19:58,571
[VOMITING]

319
00:20:00,615 --> 00:20:03,159
You were so good in Stand by Me.

320
00:20:03,326 --> 00:20:05,328
[VOMITING]

321
00:20:10,792 --> 00:20:13,586
Hello, I'm Dr. Sheldon Cooper.

322
00:20:13,753 --> 00:20:17,631
Welcome to
Sheldon Cooper Presents Fun With Flags.

323
00:20:18,967 --> 00:20:20,885
Get ready for a very special episode...

324
00:20:21,052 --> 00:20:24,972
...where we explore the flags of the popular
entertainment franchise Star Trek.

325
00:20:25,140 --> 00:20:28,560
And to help us,
I'm pleased to introduce a special guest.

326
00:20:28,727 --> 00:20:33,148
Surprisingly, it only took gas money and
the promise of free food to get him here.

327
00:20:33,314 --> 00:20:35,482
Mr. LeVar Burton.

328
00:20:37,026 --> 00:20:38,944
Hey, Sheldon. It's a pleasure to be here.

329
00:20:39,112 --> 00:20:42,406
-Well, we've got some interesting flags--
-Cut.

330
00:20:43,658 --> 00:20:46,535
Yikes, this guy is worse than Wil Wheaton.

331
00:20:50,123 --> 00:20:53,584
I don't know what she's talking about,
but I'm obligated to agree with her.

332
00:20:53,752 --> 00:20:56,921
-She's my girlfriend.
-Ah. I hear you, brother.

333
00:20:57,088 --> 00:20:59,381
I still get lunch, right?

334
00:21:32,582 --> 00:21:34,584
[English - US - SDH]

